<WorkLayout title="How we evaluate courses | SSEGU Work" description="Our evidence standards for course access, credentials and employability guidance.">
  <main class="work-page-shell work-detail-body">
    <p class="work-eyebrow">About this catalogue</p><h1>How we evaluate courses</h1>
    <p>We distinguish provider facts, dated job-market evidence and editorial assessment. A working link alone does not verify a course or its career value.</p>
    <h2>Evidence labels</h2><ul><li><strong>Verified:</strong> directly checked against an authoritative source.</li><li><strong>Supported:</strong> backed by multiple relevant sources or dated job postings.</li><li><strong>Editorial assessment:</strong> our reasoned interpretation, separated from provider claims.</li><li><strong>Not verified:</strong> unknown or unchecked; never presented as fact.</li></ul>
    <h2>Access and credentials</h2><p>Learning access, graded assessment, certificates, digital badges and professional exams are separate. Prices and regional availability are dated and checked with the provider; Uganda checkout details are not assumed from US pricing.</p>
    <h2>Employability</h2><p>Course completion does not guarantee a job, salary, promotion or freelance income. Profiles should describe plausible uses, additional skill gaps and practical evidence a learner can build.</p>
    <p>Editorial research is tracked internally by course, including its evidence completeness, last verification date and remaining work.</p>
  </main>
</WorkLayout>
